The inclusion of "cats" in the task graph introduces ambiguity because it can lead to incorrect counting of fruits. The query specifically mentions "peach," "three cats," and "a raspberry." While "cats" are not fruits, their mention could be interpreted as part of the count if the task is not clearly defined to focus only on fruits.

To address this issue, the task graph should explicitly filter out non-fruit items. A revised version might look like:

```json
{
    "owner_agent": "MetricMaestro",
    "tasks": {
        "CountFruits": "Count the number of fruits mentioned in the user query.",
        "FilterNonFruitItems": "Remove any non-fruit items from the list before counting."
    },
    "orders": [
        {
            "condition": "success",
            "from": "CountFruits",
            "to": "End"
        }
    ],
    "refused": false,
    "answer": null
}
```

This ensures that only fruits are counted, avoiding any confusion caused by non-fruit items like "cats."
